{
  "title": "Stable headers shouldn't use anonymous namespaces",
  "issue_id": "163343",
  "bug_description": "### 🐛 Describe the bug\n\nSome of the headers of the stable API have anonymous namespaces inside of them:\nhttps://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/264e7f68a095b5b2f10e7ca66a3bbb16f6e56e28/torch/csrc/stable/stableivalue_conversions.h#L11-L13\n\nThis is considered an [anti-pattern](https://clang.llvm.org/extra/clang-tidy/checks/misc/use-anonymous-namespace.html), and it has the side effect that the global `to` and `from` names are overloaded in every file that includes those headers.\n\nI'm not sure whether I fully grasp the original reason for using an anonymous namespace, but I wonder whether an anonymous namespace _inside_ a named namespace would work. Something like this:\n```cpp\nnamespace torch::stable {\nnamespace {\ntemplate <typename T>\nStableIValue from(T val);\ntemplate <typename T>\nT to(StableIValue val);\n}\n}\n```\n\n### Versions\n\nPyTorch nightly from 2025-09-05",
